docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_systems_sixteenth/SCOUT_REPORT.md:25:| CNL: binary word XOR its least cyclic rotation | Zero is the unique fixed point. At power-of-two length n, F^n=0 follows from the P178 augmentation-filtration template; it is not a new sharp clock. Every odd n >= 3 has nontrivial cycles, but no complete all-length temporal atlas is proved. Every target has at most one source per necklace; zero is the unique maximal target with the necklace-count fibre. This inverse maximum is generic canonical-section subtraction. | NO_PROMOTION / HOLD_GLOBAL_TEMPORAL; missing global axis and spent partial engines |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_systems_sixteenth/SCOUT_REPORT.md:26:| D2LC: complement at the least degree-two graph vertex | Full all-n recurrent test, exact per-state entry rule, sharp maximum 0,0,1,2,2,... for n=1,2,3,4,5,...; degree-only exact inverse for every target; maximum fibre 3 for n>=3 with every equality target characterized. P200 consumes the monotone-priority involution core. Residual forward behaviour is an at-most-four-vertex decorated local machine; inverse choices are confined to the least active target and its two neighbours. | NO_PROMOTION / KILL_BOUNDED_LOCAL_PRIORITY_GADGET |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_systems_sixteenth/SCOUT_REPORT.md:27:| LRG: least row rotations followed by greatest column rotations | Content preservation and one-dimensional idempotence proved. Eight finite boxes are idempotent, but neither all-shape temporal/core nor a separate all-shape inverse theorem is proved. Old whole-row/column lexical sorting is a different rule and cannot fill the gap. | NO_PROMOTION / HOLD_ALL_SHAPE_PROOF |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_systems_sixteenth/SCOUT_REPORT.md:28:| LIR: reverse values at the lex-first longest increasing subsequence | Inversion count strictly rises until the reverse permutation; coarse binomial clock and admissible-subsequence inverse give only the old sorting-potential shell. No sharp global time or fibre extremum is proved. | NO_PROMOTION / KILL_SORTING_POTENTIAL_ONLY; desk-only |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_systems_sixteenth/SCOUT_REPORT.md:29:| LMH: move the leftmost misplaced value to its home position, shifting others | Elizalde–Winkler Section 5 directly owns the sharp 2^(n-1)-1 clock and the exact scheduler's extremizer. Reverse placement plus selector filtering is not a separate new inverse mechanism. | NO_PROMOTION / KILL_DIRECT_TEMPORAL_OWNER; desk-only |
docs/papers204_208_sequence/scouting/finite_systems_sixteenth/SCOUT_REPORT.md:30:| KFR: first lex-increasing ternary Knuth triple rewrite | Eight exact oriented rules give generic finite-order termination and pattern-avoidance fixed states; classical Knuth invariance does not give confluence or a new inverse extremum. | NO_PROMOTION / KILL_ORDERED_KNUTH_REWRITE_SHELL; desk-only |
